---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/privy-vs-justuno';
const title = 'Privy vs Justuno for Shopify: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare Privy and Justuno for Shopify list growth: a controlled onsite offer test, subscriber quality, ESP handoffs and operating costs.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How should a small Shopify team choose?",
    "answer": "Compare the complete capture-to-message task and the operator time it requires. Revenue alone cannot determine fit."
  },
  {
    "question": "How does pricing compare?",
    "answer": "Request current quotes for the intended onsite scope, channels, support and downstream sender. Model the traffic and contact assumptions explicitly."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which has better popup conversion rates?",
    "answer": "No comparative result is established here. Test equivalent offers and eligible audiences, then examine subscriber quality and purchases."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can either replace an email platform?",
    "answer": "Privy offers email and SMS as well as list growth. Evaluate Justuno around its onsite role and demonstrate the chosen downstream sender; do not assume identical email scope."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also consider Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "It can enter the email evaluation if it meets your delivery, data and suppression needs. A separate sender adds a handoff that must be justified."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which has better popup testing?",
    "answer": "Justuno documents A/B testing; compare the exact assignment, targeting and reporting controls you require in both trials."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which integrates with Shopify more cleanly?",
    "answer": "Test the live data path, mobile storefront and preference updates. A catalog listing alone does not establish your field mappings or reliability."
  },
  {
    "question": "What test should decide?",
    "answer": "Use an equivalent sizing-guide offer, inspect mobile behavior and trace new, repeated and suppressed submissions through the chosen sender."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Privy vs Justuno</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Privy vs Justuno for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-cyan-100">A store comparing Privy with Justuno needs to decide how it will improve onsite offers and deliver what each signup was promised. Privy combines list growth with email and SMS. Justuno positions its popup tooling around design, targeting and testing. Evaluate the capture-to-message path, including the downstream sender, rather than assuming both products are temporary email platforms.</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-cyan-100/90">This is a requirements comparison with proposed exercises, not a hands-on performance study. SMS scope, destination eligibility and support need confirmation for the selected account when used.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="mt-12 card overflow-x-auto">
        <h2 class="px-5 py-4 font-serif text-2xl font-black text-white">Comparison at a glance</h2>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Privy</th><th>Justuno</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Evaluation scope</td><td>Capture plus owned email/SMS workflows</td><td>Onsite experience plus the chosen messaging integration</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Offer design</td><td>Test the required display and targeting</td><td>Test the same offer, timing and targeting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Experiment</td><td>Record assignment and eligible visitors</td><td>Record assignment and eligible visitors</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Handoff</td><td>May send the promised message itself</td><td>Prove delivery to the selected email platform</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cost inputs</td><td>Selected channels, support and contacts</td><td>Quoted onsite scope plus downstream sender and integration</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Choose the experiment before choosing the popup</h2>
        <p>Justuno documents popup targeting and A/B testing. Those capabilities do not establish a higher conversion rate or make a gamified offer suitable for every brand. Privy also has a capture role and can own subsequent messaging. A useful comparison specifies the offer, eligible visitor, destination and success metric before looking at template galleries.</p>
        <h2>Proposed exercise: a jewelry sizing guide</h2>
        <p>Offer a ring-sizing guide to visitors viewing rings, while keeping a separate newsletter signup available elsewhere. The form should explain what will arrive and avoid suggesting that a guide request automatically expresses interest in every promotion. This is a proposed store exercise, not an observed jewelry merchant case study.</p>
        <h2>Control placement and incentive</h2>
        <p>Use equivalent guide copy, placement, delay and eligibility in both trials. Do not compare an exit overlay with a footer form or a percentage discount with a non-discount guide and attribute the difference to software. Check a returning subscriber, a recent purchaser and a visitor who already dismissed the offer. Confirm whether the required exclusion can actually be configured in your selected plan.</p>
        <h2>Check small-screen behavior before measuring signups</h2>
        <p>On a narrow screen, open the size chart, focus the form, use the keyboard and dismiss the overlay. Inspect whether the visitor can return to the product selection without losing context. Repeat with another active banner so competing overlays are visible. Record failures by device and page; a higher signup total cannot excuse blocking the purchase task.</p>
        <h2>Follow the guide into the downstream sender</h2>
        <p>Submit a new address, resubmit it and then update its preferences. Confirm that the guide arrives once and that the source remains identifiable for later analysis. Justuno has messaging integrations, but the specific connector must preserve your selected fields and suppression state. If Privy sends the guide itself, inspect the same sequence rather than assuming a single vendor removes every duplication risk.</p>
        <h2>Measure qualified acquisition fairly</h2>
        <p>Record eligible visitors, submissions, confirmed reachable addresses and subsequent purchases using a consistent observation period. Keep existing customers separate from newly acquired subscribers. Random assignment and sufficient traffic matter more than a fixed two-week rule. If the storefront cannot run equivalent simultaneous variants, document time and traffic differences so sequential results are not presented as causal proof.</p>
        <h2>Model discount economics only when the offer uses one</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical discount test, assume 100 acquired subscribers produce ten orders with $30 contribution each before acquisition incentives. If those ten orders each use a $5 incentive, contribution is $300 minus $50, or $250, before tool and labor costs. This does not estimate a real store outcome. Compare guide and discount cohorts using net contribution and repeat behavior, rather than rewarding a larger unqualified list.</p>
        <h2>Account for the sender and the experiment owner</h2>
        <p>Get quotes for the actual onsite features, traffic assumptions, selected email/SMS products and support. Include the downstream sender in a Justuno-led architecture. Ask who configures targeting, reviews experiment assignments and fixes a broken field mapping. Retain two vendors only if that ownership is workable and the onsite benefit merits the added operating work.</p>
        <h2>Decision and additional email options</h2>
        <p>Prefer Privy when the integrated capture-to-message trial meets the requirements with manageable effort. Prefer a Justuno-led capture layer when its demonstrated onsite controls matter enough to justify the separate sender. Sequenzy can be considered for email if it passes the exact guide delivery and suppression requirements; it is not a predetermined graduation step. Neither order volume nor a signup lift percentage defines a universal migration point.</p>
        <h2>Product references and limits</h2>
        <p><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/">Privy product scope</a> · <a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/integrations">Privy connectors</a> · <a class="link" href="https://www.justuno.com/popups">Justuno popup tools</a> · <a class="link" href="https://mailchimp.com/integrations/justuno/">Justuno messaging integration example</a>. Product documentation establishes advertised scope, not your account configuration, comparative performance or a guaranteed implementation. Privy also offers expert assistance; confirm the actual work included rather than assuming managed execution.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-privy">Omnisend vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-privy">Sequenzy vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-privy">Klaviyo vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Privy vs Justuno FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
